WEBVTT

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.090
<i>I've decided... what I'm going to get.</i>

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:38.220
Did you find anything that you liked, miss?

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:41.530
If you're interested, we also 
have this year's hottest styles.

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:43.230
Um... Uh...

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:46.460
Someone as pretty as you 
would look good in anything!

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:47.730
Huh? Um...

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:50.130
M-Maybe next time!

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:51.150
Huh?

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:55.170
You can't be so pushy with that customer!

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.030
What?

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.960
First, we need to begin 
finalizing the protagonist, Peco.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:32.360
Right!

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:36.960
We'll be asked to make revisions 
down to the finest details

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:40.760
or possibly even to redraw everything.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.390
So finish early, and be ready to redo it.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:45.000
Just leave it to me!

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.130
Is she going to be okay?

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:58.360
It's already in 3D!

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:04.330
This is the test model... 
that'll be used in the prototype.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:05.930
I see.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:10.400
Um, if you have any questions regarding 
the design, don't hesitate to ask!

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:11.270
Okay.

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:23.450
Don't hesitate at all!

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:24.600
Huh? Wha...?

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:29.310
N-No... I really don't have anything...

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:32.090
I see...

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:37.490
It's just, this is the first time someone else 
has modeled one of my designs,

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:41.120
so I thought you might want to 
ask me about the shapes

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.840
or parts that you can't get to work in 3D.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:47.350
I don't really have...
 any questions like that...

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:48.990
Oh!

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:53.360
The design's so simple that 
I can't take any shortcuts,

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:54.500
so that's difficult!

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:58.460
I'll keep that in mind for next time...

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:00.630
What are you doing?

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.890
You have to get going on those designs.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:05.800
I'm sorry.

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:08.300
How are things going, Hifumin?

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.470
Okay.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:12.670
Oh, yeah. About this part...

00:04:13.090 --> 00:04:16.560
What do you want to do 
about the plushies' texture?

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.820
Should we use fur?

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:21.140
Hmm... I'm not sure.

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:23.570
We're going for a more cel-shaded look.

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:26.320
If you have any design 
questions, just ask me!

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:31.340
Well, sure, but you don't even know 
that much about 3D yet, do you?

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:35.780
B-But I <i>have</i> done a year's worth of it...

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:37.850
Yep. <i>Just</i> one year.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.750
Well, whatever.

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:44.560
So about using fur for the texture.

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:46.090
What do you think?

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:49.420
What's "fur" mean, here?

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:51.370
What did I tell you?

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:55.100
"Fur" here is... to demonstrate...

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.860
This isn't final, so it might look weird.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:04:59.080
Generating fur...

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:03.620
It looks like this. We can simulate 
a fur texture realistically.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:09.310
So fluffy! Great, let's use it!

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:11.500
Well...

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:13.460
O-One second, please.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:16.210
I'm against the fur.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:17.080
Huh?

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:21.710
The specs call for lots of the bear monsters 
to be onscreen at the same time.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:26.230
The fur is more realistic, but too much of it
causes lag and rendering issues.

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:28.510
There are too many problems with it.

00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:31.830
Yeah, you've got a point.

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:32.760
Oh, yeah.

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:37.280
In <i>Fairies</i>, your furry monsters
didn't use the fur effect, right?

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:41.230
Right. I only use it when 
I absolutely have to.

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:43.400
There are other ways to get the same look.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:46.360
Really? Could you show us?

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:47.580
Sure.

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:50.700
Character Team

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:50.720
Takimoto Hifumi
Yagami Ko
Iijima Yun
Suzukaze Aoba
Shinoda Hajime - Shortcut

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:53.910
File               Home           Shared         Display

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:52.850
This is based on something 
I thought worked well

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:52.450
Iijima Yun

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:52.450
_Fairies Story 2
_Fairies Story 3
_Peco(working title)
Scans
Reference materials
New Folder
Design sheets

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:53.910
_Fairies Story 3

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:53.910
Chimera Ant
Gorm
Mr Catfish
Phantom Horse
Naijoshi
Balloon Demon

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:55.290
in a computer-animated movie I watched.

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:58.170
Oh, it's what you used for this creature.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:05:59.240
That's right.

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:04.740
Come on, Aoba. You're going to 
be doing more 3D work, too.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:06.420
Pay attention to Yun's explanation.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:07.880
R-Right!

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:12.170
So this is what the texture looks like.

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:13.430
I see.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:17.310
The colors are sharp and realistic.

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:20.160
H-How did you make this?

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:21.520
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:24.090
I just scanned a blanket I had 
at home and applied some filters.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.640
<i>I can't contribute any opinions.</i>

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:26.980
Ooh, I see...

00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:29.560
<i>This is a character that I designed...</i>

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:30.560
Hey, could you make it look more ruffled?

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:32.410
<i>I need to say </i>something<i>.</i>

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:34.300
Ruffled? Hmm...

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:35.790
<i>Something insightful...</i>

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:39.650
<i>Quickly... Anything!</i>

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:44.010
<i>I'm supposed to be the character designer...</i>

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:55.870
If you give me a little time, 
I can make some more samples.

00:06:55.870 --> 00:06:57.850
Really? Then, please do.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:01.940
Oh, it's almost lunchtime. 
We can pick this up again afterwards.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:03.650
Okay, got it.

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:08.530
A-Aoba-chan...?

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:10.490
Yes?

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:12.840
Um, uh...

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:17.040
Do you want to go get lunch together?!

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:18.060
Huh?!

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:20.790
Uh, sure!

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:33.980
Until recently, I never would have thought 
you'd be the one to invite me.

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:34.850
Yeah.

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:37.990
I'm trying to get better...

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:40.410
at being conversational...

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:42.190
a little at a time...

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:46.210
I see! So that's why you invited me to lunch.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:48.100
But today...

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:51.700
was because I was 
worried about you, Aoba-chan!

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:59.580
You were acting... 
like something... was wrong...

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.480
Was I that obvious?

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:06.340
I couldn't contribute to 
the discussion at all earlier.

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:11.090
I'm supposed to be the character designer, 
but I couldn't be of any help.

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:14.330
I'm useless.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:22.440
And as if that wasn't enough, 
now I'm having a pity party...

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:23.560
Th-That's not it!

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:28.260
I was trying to think of 
what to say. S-Sorry...

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:31.280
I'm not very good at voicing 
my opinions either...

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:34.030
So, um...

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:41.240
I understand how it feels to panic like that.

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:46.580
You do?

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:48.150
So...

00:08:48.990 --> 00:08:55.010
I don't feel as though... 
you're not of any help.

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:58.040
And your design is really cute...

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:01.010
Hifumi-senpai...

00:09:01.010 --> 00:09:04.260
Not to mention, you can't 
contribute to the 3D discussions

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:06.110
because you're still inexperienced!

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:07.150
It's only obvious!

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:10.150
<b>Obvious</b>

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:10.150
Oh... Sorry!

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:13.390
You're right...

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:17.050
I must have just gotten 
this silly notion in my head

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:21.250
that I could do anything now that 
I was a character designer.

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:26.050
Even though I had no reason to assume that.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:30.340
Ooh, I'm so embarrassed!

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:32.840
I still have a lot to learn!

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:36.050
Yeah...

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:37.850
Let's do our best, together.

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:43.370
Um... Please continue to mentor me!

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:45.210
Sure, you got it!

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:47.730
All right, let's get right back into it...

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:49.130
Er, what?

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:51.230
What's wrong, Hifumi-senpai?!

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:56.610
Exhausted... from talking too much...

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:58.820
Can't... go on!

00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:02.700
What?! But you just said 
we should do our best together!

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:13.300
Okay! The game's really coming along now.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:16.300
Dragon fire... implemented!

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:19.340
<b>This application has stopped working</b>

00:10:22.170 --> 00:10:23.730
Ahagon.

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:26.650
How's that feature coming along?

00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:29.040
How many times must I tell you it's Umiko?

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:31.950
And I'm actually about to finish right now.

00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:35.360
<b>This application has stopped working</b>

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:39.950
Rubelle's

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:39.950
Beginner's Course

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:41.410
Oh, I get it!

00:10:42.090 --> 00:10:43.450
This should...

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:45.200
Tap!

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:48.620
Hooray!

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:50.670
I just made a minor mistake.

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:53.000
Are you sure?

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:55.090
This should...

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:55.550
Tap.

00:10:57.660 --> 00:11:00.970
Looking good! It burned away real nice.

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:02.580
This is nothing.

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:05.470
Please adjust the details of 
the appearance on your end.

00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:08.680
Wow! It's breathing fire.

00:11:09.380 --> 00:11:12.190
I know, right? I worked really hard!

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:16.130
I'm programming it from scratch, 
without using a game engine!

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:17.230
Really?

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:19.410
Oh, yeah.

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:23.090
I found a part-time job that pays 
pretty well. Want to do it with me?

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:27.770
I'm busy with this right now, so I'll pass.

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:29.260
What are you angry about?

00:11:29.260 --> 00:11:30.370
I'm not angry!

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:33.380
Okay, I get it.

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:36.110
You're having fun with that right now.

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:38.380
But if you change your mind, let me know.

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:41.510
Sorry...

00:11:42.780 --> 00:11:47.760
It sure is hard to genuinely impress someone.

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:49.960
I have to make it even better!

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:54.530
It's a good effect.

00:11:54.530 --> 00:11:58.650
By the way, how many of those can 
burn at once before it starts to lag?

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:00.900
Probably around ten.

00:12:02.440 --> 00:12:05.310
Now, 100... is more than I'll ask for,

00:12:05.310 --> 00:12:11.080
but could you optimize it enough 
to handle 20 or 30 burning at once?

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:14.830
I see that you're as 
difficult to please as ever.

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:17.420
But of course.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:18.590
And besides...

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:22.160
I get to see the face you 
make under pressure!

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:24.340
Do you want me to improve this or not?

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:29.350
How about... this?

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:34.350
That looks a bit better!

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:41.400
That should about do it.

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:52.180
Well, that ought to be acceptable.

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:58.370
I'm so tired! My head feels 
like it's going to burst!

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:02.400
I've made a lot more progress,

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:06.550
so I wonder if Umiko-san would give 
me advice if I showed it to her.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:10.750
Such revolutionary code... 
Are you some kind of genius?

00:13:10.750 --> 00:13:13.180
JK! But wait...

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:15.830
Is that all?

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:18.900
What if she says that instead? I'm scared...

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:24.890
Well, I think I can head home for the day.

00:13:26.150 --> 00:13:28.570
<b>Sakura Nene</b>

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:31.310
Hello, this is Umiko.

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:34.330
It's been a while.

00:13:35.030 --> 00:13:35.580
Yes.

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:38.580
Certainly. I don't mind.

00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:43.350
I hadn't heard from you in so long,
I was getting worried.

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:50.810
These chocolates are good. Want one?

00:13:50.810 --> 00:13:52.150
Sure, thanks.

00:13:52.150 --> 00:13:54.610
Good morning...

00:13:54.610 --> 00:13:56.020
Oh, good morning.

00:13:56.020 --> 00:14:00.060
Why do you look so tired when it's 
only Monday? Still in weekend mode?

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:02.020
N-No, not at all!

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:04.320
Did you go out somewhere yesterday?

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:08.510
I wanted to meet up with 
Nenecchi since it's been a while,

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:13.180
but she's been busy lately, 
so I ended up just lazing around at home.

00:14:13.180 --> 00:14:15.850
Well, it's good that you got to unwind.

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:17.390
Oh, right!

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:20.250
We've got a meeting about 
the prototype before lunch,

00:14:20.680 --> 00:14:22.880
so have your materials ready, Aoba.

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:24.580
G-Got it!

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:29.090
All right! Gotta get my head in the game.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:39.060
<b>Very Delicious</b>

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:39.060
<b>Soy Milk</b>

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:39.060
Egg Salad
Sandwich

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:40.770
Ugh... The week's just started and I'm 
already exhausted from all these meetings.

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:45.230
Good work. Things seem to be 
on track for once, this time.

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:48.510
I know, right? You can praise me if you want.

00:14:48.510 --> 00:14:50.110
Yes, truly amazing...

00:14:50.670 --> 00:14:53.620
Rin-san's management abilities, that is.

00:14:54.900 --> 00:14:56.580
Oh, don't be so coy!

00:14:57.060 --> 00:14:59.490
I only told the truth.

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:05.390
Well anyway, Toyama-kun and Yagami 
have both progressed wonderfully,

00:15:05.390 --> 00:15:06.760
so I'm relieved.

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:08.470
Come to think of it,

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:13.210
it seems that Ko-san is managing 
quite well as AD this time.

00:15:13.210 --> 00:15:14.360
She sure is.

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:17.770
Though by the time I left 
my last job and came here,

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:20.680
Ko-san had already stepped down as AD,

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:23.650
so it's not like I have 
a basis of comparison.

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:28.360
I remember troubled young Yagami.

00:15:31.390 --> 00:15:33.450
She was so cute!

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:35.160
I wasn't asking about that.

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:36.350
But you see,

00:15:36.350 --> 00:15:39.780
Yagami wouldn't be 
who she is today without her past.

00:15:39.780 --> 00:15:42.110
It was necessary.

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:47.180
Aoba-chan, whatcha doing for lunch?

00:15:47.180 --> 00:15:49.600
I was going to go buy something.

00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:50.850
Then why don't we all go?

00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:53.590
I do feel bad for the ones who quit.

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:56.290
And as for who was accountable for it all,

00:15:56.290 --> 00:15:58.680
it would be me, since I was in charge.

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:05.140
So I have one rule when 
I choose who'll be working under me.

00:16:05.140 --> 00:16:06.190
And what's that?

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:12.360
I'll only take employees who are cute enough
 that I'd gladly tolerate their failures!

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:15.200
I was a fool for expecting a serious answer.

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:19.440
Come on, now. That includes you, Umiko-kun.

00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:25.500
So, that said... There's a teensy change 
I want to make to the specs...

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:30.780
Won't you tolerate my failures, too...?

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:32.660
What?

00:16:32.660 --> 00:16:36.050
We agreed to a forehead flick 
if you change the specs.

00:16:36.050 --> 00:16:38.760
W-Well, I mean...

00:16:39.110 --> 00:16:41.570
Now tolerate your forehead flick.

00:16:42.050 --> 00:16:43.180
But...

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:44.850
Forehead flick...

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:48.090
Ow!

00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:52.670
Jeez! But you know spec 
changes are inevitable!

00:16:53.210 --> 00:16:54.550
You misunderstand.

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:58.700
My forehead flicks aren't 
for changing the specs.

00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:03.960
They're for trying to 
play it off as if it's nothing.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:06.880
If you were to show 
some remorse, like Ko-san,

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:09.140
my forehead flicks would be gentler.

00:17:12.690 --> 00:17:13.640
Really?

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:15.550
That doesn't look like remorse.

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:20.850
H-Hey! Well, if it isn't my girls!

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:23.560
Oh, hello!

00:17:24.550 --> 00:17:26.980
My, that's quite the packed lunch.

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:30.520
Believe it or not, 
Hifumi-senpai brought it for us!

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:33.150
Ooh. Home cooking from Hifumi-kun?

00:17:33.150 --> 00:17:34.360
Y-Yes...

00:17:34.770 --> 00:17:37.660
I thought... we could share...

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:42.870
P-Please, help yourself.

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:46.000
How delightful. I would love some.

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:51.820
U-Um... Some are store-bought premade...

00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:57.610
Delicious! So this is how 
you flavor your omelets.

00:17:57.610 --> 00:17:59.970
Uh... actually... yes.

00:18:00.310 --> 00:18:02.810
<i>Those must've been premade.</i>

00:18:06.050 --> 00:18:07.900
A-Aoba-chan...

00:18:08.890 --> 00:18:09.810
Here...

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:12.860
I made some meat and potatoes...

00:18:15.630 --> 00:18:16.530
Have some...

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:19.530
Hey, that looks good! First bite's mine!

00:18:20.860 --> 00:18:23.170
Wow, that <i>is</i> good!

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:27.910
Oh... Sorry.

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:31.030
B-But there's still plenty, 
so no harm done, right?

00:18:31.030 --> 00:18:33.170
Not to mention, it really was good.

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:36.300
It might even be better than 
Rin's meat and potatoes.

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:42.760
Hifumi-chan, do you mind 
if I try some as well?

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:44.120
Pardon my table manners.

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:45.850
Huh? Uh...

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:49.310
So you prefer this kind of flavor, Ko-chan?

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:51.310
What are you so huffy about?

00:18:51.890 --> 00:18:55.130
Say, why don't you have some, too, Umiko-kun?

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:56.320
It's delicious.

00:18:57.540 --> 00:19:00.070
Come on. Say, "Ah."

00:19:06.310 --> 00:19:08.620
H-Huh?

00:19:10.490 --> 00:19:15.240
It is indeed delicious. 
Like something you'd buy from a store.

00:19:15.240 --> 00:19:17.130
Is something the matter?

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:20.880
E-Er, I totally thought 
you'd get embarrassed...

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:26.140
Oh, so that's what you were after. 
You have quite the one-track mind.

00:19:26.140 --> 00:19:29.370
Too bad for you, but I recently 
became acclimated to it.

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:30.570
So it's no big deal.

00:19:30.570 --> 00:19:32.960
Huh?! With who?!

00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:35.650
Why are you all reacting like that?

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:37.490
Well...

00:19:39.230 --> 00:19:40.630
It's a secret.

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:44.660
So this is your college.

00:19:46.130 --> 00:19:48.450
Are you sure that I'm allowed in?

00:19:48.450 --> 00:19:54.050
Yup! The cafeteria here has really 
good food, so let's eat there later.

00:20:02.570 --> 00:20:04.300
You've certainly worn this book out.

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:08.010
Yeah! That book's super easy to understand.

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:12.620
By the way, this book is even more beat up!

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:15.230
<b>C </b>Programming
for Beginners

00:20:12.620 --> 00:20:15.230
Did you spill coffee on it?

00:20:16.390 --> 00:20:19.150
So, what was the reason 
you wanted to meet today?

00:20:20.650 --> 00:20:27.240
The reason? Well, it's the 
same as before, but, um...

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:30.670
How unlike you to act 
so ill at ease, Sakura-san.

00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:32.500
You know the reason!

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:34.710
Then hurry up and show me.

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:40.040
Here.

00:20:44.490 --> 00:20:48.070
So now it's got a boss who breathes flames!

00:20:48.070 --> 00:20:51.020
You certainly put effort into these flames.

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:53.060
You even programmed their behavior.

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:58.280
I know, right? Aren't I amazing?

00:20:58.280 --> 00:21:00.380
I didn't compliment you that much.

00:21:00.380 --> 00:21:01.400
No way!

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:03.400
Not to mention, it's rather slow.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:06.350
You shouldn't have lag 
with graphics like this.

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:09.110
Huh? No way.

00:21:09.110 --> 00:21:10.760
Is it really?

00:21:10.760 --> 00:21:13.420
I mean, sure, it's a little jerky....

00:21:13.420 --> 00:21:16.040
However minor, it's still lag.

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:18.190
And the collision detection is shoddy.

00:21:18.190 --> 00:21:21.470
A former debugger should be 
experienced at checking that.

00:21:21.470 --> 00:21:25.000
Aw, but it's a pain to actually fix it...

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:27.140
A pain? Then do you want to quit?

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:30.180
Hey! I didn't say that I was going to quit!

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:32.100
I'll keep at it!

00:21:32.740 --> 00:21:36.310
By the way, have you 
heard about Suzukaze-san?

00:21:37.830 --> 00:21:38.560
Huh?

00:21:38.930 --> 00:21:41.320
Wow, that's amazing, Aocchi!

00:21:41.630 --> 00:21:45.190
Getting character designer as a rookie, 
just like Yagami-san!

00:21:45.190 --> 00:21:47.650
<i>I-It's not like that at all!</i>

00:21:47.650 --> 00:21:49.490
<i>I can't go into specifics,</i>

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:52.370
<i>but it's a team effort,
and I'm getting lots of help.</i>

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:55.200
<i>I've still got a ways to go.</i>

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:57.430
I see.

00:21:57.430 --> 00:21:59.890
<i>Sorry I haven't contacted you in a while.</i>

00:21:59.890 --> 00:22:02.980
It's fine. I had a lot to do.

00:22:02.980 --> 00:22:04.710
<i>Did you start a part-time job?</i>

00:22:06.900 --> 00:22:08.680
Something like that.
